{"data": [{"author_id": "593053970", "created_at": "2026-11-03T20:54:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117722206931456311"], "id": "2117722206931456311", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 61, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "every new model comes with 15 benchmark scores. here's what each group actually tests\n\nknowledge and hard reasoning\n- mmlu / mmlu-pro: school and college multiple choice\n- gpqa diamond: phd-level science questions\n- humanity's last exam: 2,500 expert questions made to be very", "url": "https://x.com/hiepremium/status/2117722206931456311"}, {"author_id": "2991448165", "created_at": "2026-11-05T06:58:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118236436596130192"], "id": "2118236436596130192", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 595, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "The current state of LLMs:\n \nOpenAI is accusing Anthropic of benchmark contamination because they lost on SWE-bench.\n\nGoogle is quietly dropping models that score 84% on ARC-AGI while everyone else argues.\n\nxAI is still trying to ship Grok 4.8 after missing the September", "url": "https://x.com/kgauravnm/status/2118236436596130192"}, {"author_id": "2030144417219366916", "created_at": "2026-11-03T21:11:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117726261803896834"], "id": "2117726261803896834", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Any benchmark that claims to test vision should have to pass this ablation. GPT-6 Luna resolved 36.9% of SWE-bench Multimodal v2 with the screenshots and 37.1% with none, while the same cut cost it 43 points on MMMU-Pro\nhttps://t.co/mu7ieZDMR7 https://t.co/wU3sKqQwyS", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/HamelHusain/st…", "end": 243, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/HamelHusain/status/2117688053129171206", "start": 220, "url": "https://t.co/mu7ieZDMR7"}, {"display_url": "x.com/825766640/stat…", "end": 267, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/825766640/status/2117688053129171206", "start": 244, "url": "https://t.co/wU3sKqQwyS"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117688053129171206", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/Contrasignal_ai/status/2117726261803896834"}, {"author_id": "991872400361836545", "created_at": "2026-11-05T01:15:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118150190494540152"], "id": "2118150190494540152", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 50, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Cognition's SWE-2 Flash is one-fifth the price and 3x the speed of SWE-2, Cognition says.\nIt edges SWE-2 on FrontierCode 2.0 (24.0 vs 23.8) but trails on every other benchmark in their table, incl. Terminal-Bench 4.0 (20.0 vs 27.3).\nWeights not public.\n#AI #AICoding #LLM https://t.co/VL53F4poST", "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 256, "start": 253, "tag": "AI"}, {"end": 266, "start": 257, "tag": "AICoding"}, {"end": 271, "start": 267, "tag": "LLM"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/VL53F4poST", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EthanLinAI/status/2118150190494540152/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118150079504920576", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/VL53F4poST"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/EthanLinAI/status/2118150190494540152"}, {"author_id": "1776256213795098624", "created_at": "2026-11-04T08:56:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117903716988903715"], "id": "2117903716988903715", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 75, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Every frontier AI model scored 0% on ProgramBench at launch.\n\nJohn Yang - the researcher behind SWE-bench, SWE-smith, and CodeClash- just dropped the benchmark that exposed the real ceiling of autonomous coding agents.\n\nHere is why it broke every model on earth:\n\nSWE-bench https://t.co/ITPgpgk6ys", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/ITPgpgk6ys", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/RSP_ER/status/2117903716988903715/video/1", "media_key": "13_2117903686622195713", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/ITPgpgk6ys"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/RSP_ER/status/2117903716988903715"}, {"author_id": "2018445924704403456", "created_at": "2026-11-04T15:37:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118004718559711332"], "id": "2118004718559711332", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "SWE-bench Multimodal, via Hamel Husain: drop the images and the score barely moves. Most tasks fall to issue text and code alone.\n\nA vision benchmark that doesn't need its images isn't testing vision. Ablate an eval's inputs before you trust it.\nhttps://t.co/B6HDtbvaoe", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/HamelHusain/st…", "end": 269, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/HamelHusain/status/2117688053129171206", "start": 246, "url": "https://t.co/B6HDtbvaoe"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117688053129171206", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/zykarys/status/2118004718559711332"}, {"author_id": "1796589647230836736", "created_at": "2026-11-04T03:46:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117825870979338346"], "id": "2117825870979338346", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 45, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Three benchmark stories in one day:\n\n- Prime Intellect found and fixed issues in popular public evals\n\n- SWE-bench Multimodal turns out to be mostly solvable without the images\n\n- AutomationBench had models describe request bodies in prose instead of JSON Schema", "url": "https://x.com/curiousalaska/status/2117825870979338346"}, {"author_id": "1524739531937021952", "created_at": "2026-11-05T06:04:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118222989762425219"], "id": "2118222989762425219", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 93, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Ripple-65B Preview is out — a 65B dense model pretrained from scratch that sets a new SOTA for U.S. open-weight models on agentic coding.\n\nIt outperforms significantly larger models (Muse Spark Open-816B, Beam-501B, Inkling-975B, Nemotron 3 Ultra-550B) while running locally on a https://t.co/KU6se7pjEX", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/RicursiveAI/st…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/RicursiveAI/status/2118046765857546733", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/KU6se7pjEX"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118046765857546733", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/rio_0xo/status/2118222989762425219"}, {"author_id": "1802341374098124800", "created_at": "2026-11-04T18:43:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118051434738717153"], "id": "2118051434738717153", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 488, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Building a good AI benchmark is quite hard. The environment, the judge, the tasks etc. \n\nfor SWE-bench Verified, 93 developers went through 1,699 tasks by hand and kept 500. a later audit still found weak tests in 26 of those 500.\n\nwe tried to automate that whole job 🧵 https://t.co/K3bncouiMN", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/K3bncouiMN", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Krrishagar/status/2118051434738717153/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118050751423578112", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/K3bncouiMN"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/Krrishagar/status/2118051434738717153"}, {"author_id": "20495560", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:03:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118388700124156016"], "id": "2118388700124156016", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 2773, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Working on an ICLR rebuttal and need to add more harness training experiments?\n\n“Can you compare against another method?”\n“Does it work with a different harness?”\n“What happens on another benchmark?”\n\nAnswering these questions often means rebuilding the same experiment pipeline https://t.co/PKrN1RR44o", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/PKrN1RR44o", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/zxlzr/status/2118388700124156016/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118388468854530048", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/PKrN1RR44o"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/PKrN1RR44o", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/zxlzr/status/2118388700124156016/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118388492480978944", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/PKrN1RR44o"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/PKrN1RR44o", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/zxlzr/status/2118388700124156016/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118388511141437441", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/PKrN1RR44o"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/PKrN1RR44o", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/zxlzr/status/2118388700124156016/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118388530187849728", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/PKrN1RR44o"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/zxlzr/status/2118388700124156016"}, {"author_id": "1496960004074713093", "created_at": "2026-11-05T04:04:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118192585189531948"], "id": "2118192585189531948", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "SWE-2 Flash costs one-fifth of SWE-2 and runs 3x faster. It also beats SWE-2 on one benchmark\n\nFrontierCode 2.0: 24.0 vs 23.8\n\nBut SWE-2 still wins on Terminal-Bench 4.0 (27.3 vs 20.0) and DeepSWE 1.1 (73.0 vs 60.1)\n\nSo here's the real play:\n- send routine work to Flash: code", "url": "https://x.com/MegaEvolvedFrog/status/2118192585189531948"}, {"author_id": "2023690746172485632", "created_at": "2026-11-04T16:03:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118011153703895518"], "id": "2118011153703895518", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Tsinghua's algebraic world model didn't just fail on ARC-AGI-3 sealed levels — it proved they're unwinnable via Lean 4 formal verification. That's a different claim than scoring low. Formal bounds on benchmark solvability is underused. #AIResearch", "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 247, "start": 236, "tag": "AIResearch"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/MorelMatth66161/status/2118011153703895518"}, {"author_id": "1948279697797988352", "created_at": "2026-11-04T19:03:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118056556407455756"], "id": "2118056556407455756", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 377, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Everyone is discussing plums about the upcoming release of Claude Opus 5.5 and Gemini 4 Argon 🧠\n\nMean CEO's BLOG - Violetta Bonenkamp\n\nHonestly, we have already passed the point where the new model surprises. Now any announcement of a neural network feels something like this:\n\n- https://t.co/ilIInq58AX", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/ilIInq58AX", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/zzaba_a/status/2118056556407455756/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118056335539359744", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/ilIInq58AX"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/ilIInq58AX", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/zzaba_a/status/2118056556407455756/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118056495149441027", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/ilIInq58AX"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/zzaba_a/status/2118056556407455756"}, {"author_id": "1852623328131112960", "created_at": "2026-11-05T13:53:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118340962237751621"], "id": "2118340962237751621", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 199, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@cognition's new coding model has 12B active parameters and scores 89.9 on SWE-Bench Pro v2 Hard. Its own flagship, SWE-2, runs 104B active and scores 90.6.\n\nThe base it started from is @thinkymachines' Inkling-Small, also 276B total and 12B active. That base scores 56.5 on the https://t.co/jSw0Rix90F", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 10, "id": "1751810001751183361", "start": 0, "username": "cognition"}, {"end": 201, "id": "1891523745929732096", "start": 186, "username": "thinkymachines"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/jSw0Rix90F", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/0xdavinci_/status/2118340962237751621/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118340955614924800", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/jSw0Rix90F"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/0xdavinci_/status/2118340962237751621"}, {"author_id": "1945887628194377729", "created_at": "2026-11-05T08:30:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118259535714328687"], "id": "2118259535714328687", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "NVIDIA’s 16K-context experiment with GPT 5.6 Sol kept SWE-bench Verified accuracy near baseline, but nominal API cost across the benchmark rose from $167.68 to $203.12, using the paper’s September prices.\n\nThe same configuration’s $40.62 cost estimate assumes lower token prices https://t.co/mN5G75GZsy", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/omarsar0/statu…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/omarsar0/status/2117956281910829083", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/mN5G75GZsy"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117956281910829083", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/open_mercury/status/2118259535714328687"}, {"author_id": "967093652576260096", "created_at": "2026-11-05T10:11:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118284949514035580"], "id": "2118284949514035580", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 226, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Wrote about model - application fit. Read it if you want to know which app categories will inflect next. https://t.co/Wj5hmDOFw6", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2118…", "end": 128, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2118282951720882176", "start": 105, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2118282951720882176", "url": "https://t.co/Wj5hmDOFw6"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/richardkeuntje/status/2118284949514035580"}, {"author_id": "2046103461846974464", "created_at": "2026-11-04T20:50:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118083430613492146"], "id": "2118083430613492146", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "SWE-2 Flash brings a 12B-active model to everyday coding\n\nCognition has released SWE-2 Flash in Devin Desktop and CLI, built on Thinking Machines’ Inkling-Small with 276B total parameters and 12B active. Cognition says it costs one-fifth as much as SWE-2 and runs three times https://t.co/PWCh0RCnug https://t.co/C0KoK1O9vJ", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/PWCh0RCnug", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AgentsPulse/status/2118083430613492146/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118083423260786688", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/PWCh0RCnug"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/PWCh0RCnug", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AgentsPulse/status/2118083430613492146/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118083423307022337", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/PWCh0RCnug"}, {"display_url": "x.com/cognition/stat…", "end": 323, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/cognition/status/2118069629713305678", "start": 300, "url": "https://t.co/C0KoK1O9vJ"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118069629713305678", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/AgentsPulse/status/2118083430613492146"}, {"author_id": "27454144", "created_at": "2026-11-05T09:24:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118273190300373471"], "id": "2118273190300373471", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 204, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Task-Efficient Agent Evaluation Using Cached Traces : https://t.co/ruTTJCPogP\n\n\"Task-efficient agent evaluation using cached traces\nBen JohnsonJatawareHayden HelmCorresponding author: hayden@helivan.ioHelivan\nAbstract\nEfficient benchmarking estimates a system’s full benchmark", "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Efficient benchmarking estimates a system's full benchmark performance from a small number of task executions. Standard approaches rely solely on the binary correctness of executions from a...", "display_url": "arxiv.org/abs/2611.06803", "end": 77, "expanded_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06803", "images": [{"height": 1000, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118272948960215040/Ju_nmZiS?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1000}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118272948960215040/Ju_nmZiS?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 54, "status": 200, "title": "Task-Efficient Agent Evaluation Using Cached Traces", "unwound_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06803", "url": "https://t.co/ruTTJCPogP"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/arnaudmercier/status/2118273190300373471"}, {"author_id": "27454144", "created_at": "2026-11-05T09:23:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118272949245329648"], "id": "2118272949245329648", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 180, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Task-Efficient Agent Evaluation Using Cached Traces : https://t.co/ruTTJCPogP\n\n\"Task-efficient agent evaluation using cached traces\nBen JohnsonJatawareHayden HelmCorresponding author: hayden@helivan.ioHelivan\nAbstract\nEfficient benchmarking estimates a system’s full benchmark", "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Efficient benchmarking estimates a system's full benchmark performance from a small number of task executions. Standard approaches rely solely on the binary correctness of executions from a...", "display_url": "arxiv.org/abs/2611.06803", "end": 77, "expanded_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06803", "images": [{"height": 1000, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118272948960215040/Ju_nmZiS?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1000}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118272948960215040/Ju_nmZiS?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 54, "status": 200, "title": "Task-Efficient Agent Evaluation Using Cached Traces", "unwound_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06803", "url": "https://t.co/ruTTJCPogP"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/arnaudmercier/status/2118272949245329648"}, {"author_id": "1149586194", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:31:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118395761146691911"], "id": "2118395761146691911", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 272, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "SWE-2 Flash just proved that raw size is no longer the binding constraint on coding models.\n\nA system with only 12 billion active parameters beat larger American open-weight models on FrontierCode, DeepSWE, and Terminal-Bench while running three times faster and at one-fifth the https://t.co/nCEcjCfEiC https://t.co/EoxTW2s6bA", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/nCEcjCfEiC", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Josephyala/status/2118395761146691911/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118395745287933952", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/nCEcjCfEiC"}, {"display_url": "x.com/cognition/stat…", "end": 327, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/cognition/status/2118069614521241739", "start": 304, "url": "https://t.co/EoxTW2s6bA"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118069614521241739", "type": "quo